# Installed by bin/setup-buildroot.
#
# devtools needs root: arch-nspawn and makechrootpkg create and enter the
# container. The pipeline itself must not run as root -- it works in the build
# user's git clones and signs with that user's GPG and SSH keys -- so these two
# commands are the only place where it escalates.
#
# This is a convenience boundary, not a security boundary. Whoever may run
# makechrootpkg against a chroot they can write to is root in practice. The
# arguments are pinned so that a mistake in the pipeline cannot reach a
# different chroot, and so that a rule that no longer matches fails loudly:
# the pipeline calls sudo with -n, which turns a mismatch into an immediate
# error instead of a password prompt that would hang an unattended run until
# its 20-hour timeout.
#
# Both lines must stay in step with update_buildroot() and build_in_chroot()
# in bin/build-ditana-packages.
#
# aurto ships an equivalent but unpinned rule for %wheel on the same machines.
# Do not rely on it: a build host has to work without aurto installed.

%wheel ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/arch-nspawn -C /etc/ditana/pacman-buildroot.conf /var/lib/ditana-buildroot/root pacman -Syu --noconfirm
%wheel ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/makechrootpkg -c -u -r /var/lib/ditana-buildroot -- -f --noconfirm --needed
